35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial cut readmissions by a fifth. It worked, but only while it was actively staffed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The car park is full by eleven. The shuttle misses most villages. There is no physical room for more.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The joint clinic died because neither side would own the rota. The data agreements take fourteen months to sign.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The therapy team is hollowed out. Midwifery has slack, but the wards are running on agency cover.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,The ledger is thinner than we thought. And the fund pays nothing for work done off site.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Servas, if the fund pays nothing for off-site work, the call-back trial is a dead end.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, even if it paid, the booking system has no slot for it. It would vanish from the records.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, if the wards are on agency cover, any new program is just a promise we cannot keep.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Benjamin, the therapy team is gone. Midwifery has slack, but the wards are drowning.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,The money is gone. The space is gone. The staff is gone. What is left?,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"The call-back trial worked, but it needs a home. The booking system has no slot for it.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The shared nursing round has no fixed appointment. It would be invisible to the system.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The midwifery program has slack. It is on-site. It does not need a data agreement.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"The midwifery program fits the slack. The wards are drowning, but midwifery has room.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,The midwifery program is on-site. It bills at the standard rate. It does not need a data agreement.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,The midwifery program has evidence. It fits the slack. It is on-site.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,The midwifery program uses existing rooms. It does not strain the car park. It fits.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,The midwifery program has no external dependency. It is owned by one department. It will not break.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,The midwifery program gives the therapy team a break. It uses the slack. It is kind.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,The midwifery program is the only one that pays for itself. It is the only one that will still be here in a year.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
